NAME
     sort - sort lines

SYNOPSIS
     sort [-n] [-r] [-u] [-f] [-k N] [-t SEP] [-o FILE] [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
     sort reads all its input, sorts the lines and writes them out.

OPTIONS
     -n        compare as numbers
     -r        reverse
     -u        one of each
     -f        ignore case
     -k N      sort on field N
     -t SEP    fields are separated by SEP rather than by whitespace
     -o FILE   write there instead of to standard output

SEE ALSO
     uniq(1), comm(1), join(1)
